.TH "WINDOW.BLUR_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Window.blur_event \- Window: blur event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]blur\f[B]\f[R] event fires when the window has lost
focus, for example when the user moves focus from the page to the
address bar.
Focus may previously have been on the document\(cqs viewport or on an
element within it.
.PP
The opposite of \f[CR]blur\f[R] is \f[CR]focus\f[R].
.PP
This event is not cancelable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqblur\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onblur = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]FocusEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]UIEvent\f[R] and \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Live example
This example changes the appearance of a document when it loses focus.
It uses \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R] to monitor \f[CR]focus\f[R] and
\f[CR]blur\f[R] events.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]p\f[R] id=\(dqlog\(dq>Click on this document to give it focus.</\f[B]p\f[R]>
.EE
.SS CSS
.IP
.EX
\&.paused {
  \f[B]background\f[R]: #dddddd;
  \f[B]color\f[R]: #555555;
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] log = document.getElementById(\(dqlog\(dq);

\f[B]function\f[R] pause() {
  document.body.classList.add(\(dqpaused\(dq);
  log.textContent = \(dqFOCUS LOST!\(dq;
}

\f[B]function\f[R] play() {
  document.body.classList.remove(\(dqpaused\(dq);
  log.textContent =
    \(dqThis document has focus. Click outside the document to lose focus.\(dq;
}

window.addEventListener(\(dqblur\(dq, pause);
window.addEventListener(\(dqfocus\(dq, play);
.EE
.SS Result
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Related event: \f[CR]focus\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
